<metadata><name>Lost Prairie and Heart Lake</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:242-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.404500" lon="-122.075626"><ele>1028.7</ele><name>Lost Prairie Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:lost-prairie-sno-park (OSM node 40211893 on US 20); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 244; book_elev_ft: 3360; quote: Start skiing at Lost Prairie Sno-Park, going west on a marked route through a meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.403370" lon="-122.077950"><ele>1029.7</ele><name>Tombstone Prairie Connection, east end</name><desc>source: USFS EDW trail SNO-4145 TOMBSTONE PRAIRIE CONNECTION, east end at Lost Prairie; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 244; quote: going west on a marked route through a meadow, enter forest, go 200 yards</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.385460" lon="-122.101990"><ele>1163.7</ele><name>Junction of Tombstone Prairie and Heart Lake Trails (roads 2000061 / 2000060)</name><desc>source: start of USFS road 2000061 on road 2000060 HEART LAKE RD; SNO-4145 turns here; confidence: high; pdf_page: 244; book_elev_ft: 3816; quote: After 2.1 miles and at 460 feet above the sno-park join you will reach the Tombstone Pass and Heart Lake Trails, both roads. Turn left (east)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.399520" lon="-122.071430"><ele>1224.6</ele><name>End of Heart Lake Trail (road 2000060 east end)</name><desc>source: east end of USFS road 2000060 HEART LAKE RD; confidence: high; pdf_page: 244; book_elev_ft: 3993; quote: follow the narrower, winding road 2.2 miles to its end in a large clearcut</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Lost Prairie and Heart Lake</name><desc>1. Lost Prairie Sno-Park -&gt; Tombstone Prairie Connection, east end: straight (medium), 0.14 mi | 2. Tombstone Prairie Connection, east end -&gt; Junction of Tombstone Prairie and Heart Lake Trails (roads 2000061 / 2000060): usfs-trail (high), 2.05 mi | 3. Junction of Tombstone Prairie and Heart Lake Trails (roads 2000061 / 2000060) -&gt; End of Heart Lake Trail (road 2000060 east end): usfs-road (high), 2.25 mi</desc>
